# Full test suite

From `build/Release`, before any commit and after a feature is finished:

```bash
ctest -Q --output-on-failure
```

Use `-Q` by default so only the summary and failures show (cuts per-test
clutter). Keep `--output-on-failure` so failing tests still dump their logs.

Re-run `cmake` in that directory when tests were added or the tree was
reconfigured. All tests must pass. A green `qumode-*` subset is not enough when
the change touches `QasmParser.y`, `QasmScanner.l`, or a shared AST builder.

After editing `lib/Parser/QasmParser.y` or `QasmScanner.l`, rebuild `QasmParser`.
Those sources are dependencies of the generated parser and scanner.
